id: SEC-041
title: OWASP Top 10 — A05 Injection (SQL, XSS, Template)
category: security
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .js .tsx .jsx .py .java .go .cpp .h
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ vendor/ _test.go
patterns:
  - regex: ` \+ req\.
    message: "A05 SQL concatenation with request data — use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection"
  - regex: \" \+ req\.
    message: "A05 SQL concatenation with request data — use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection"
  - regex: f\"SELECT
    message: "A05 SQL f-string interpolation — use parameterized queries, not string formatting"
  - regex: \$\{req\.
    message: "A05 Template injection — user input in template literal enables code execution"
  - regex: innerHTML
    message: "A05 XSS via innerHTML — use textContent or a sanitizer (DOMPurify) instead"
  - regex: dangerouslySetInnerHTML
    message: "A05 XSS in React — dangerouslySetInnerHTML bypasses React's XSS protection. Sanitize with DOMPurify"
  - regex: document\.write
    message: "A05 XSS via document.write — use DOM APIs (createElement/textContent) instead"
fix: Use parameterized queries for SQL. Use textContent instead of innerHTML. Sanitize HTML with DOMPurify. Never interpolate user input into templates or queries.
